          Do I own my website?
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">On the monthly subscription, I own the code and host it for you, which is how the site can launch with no money down on your end. The arrangement is similar to leasing a storefront, in that you get the benefit of the space without the up-front capital outlay. If you ever decide to take the site elsewhere, I will provide a clean static export of the live site that runs on any host with no dependencies attached.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
          Why not just use WordPress, Wix, Squarespace, or an AI builder?
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">WordPress is the most-targeted platform on the internet, and its page builders generate slow, bloated code on top of that. Wix and Squarespace work fine for an absolute beginner who just needs something live, but they cap you on speed, on visual uniqueness, and on the local-SEO depth that service businesses depend on. AI page builders produce sites that look done in the editor and perform poorly in the real world, and once they are live, no one can really tell you why the phone is not ringing. I custom-code every site from scratch and stay with the work after launch, which is why the result is faster, more secure, and unmistakably your business rather than a template anyone else could buy.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
          How long does it take to build my site?
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">Most sites are designed, built, and launched within two to three weeks of the discovery call. We start with that call, then I send a design preview for your review, and once you have signed off I finalize the build and ship it live. The faster you can send the content I need from your side, the logo, the photos, the body copy, the faster the whole thing comes together.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
          What if I need changes after the site launches?
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">Unlimited content updates are part of the standard plan and always will be. If you need to change your hours, add a service, swap out a team photo, or run a seasonal callout, you simply email or text me and the change moves quickly on most business days. Anything genuinely outside the standard scope, like a custom-built calculator, a third-party booking integration, or a data migration, is billed at a flat one hundred dollars an hour with a written estimate before I start, never as a surprise on an invoice.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-more">
      <a href="/faq/" class="btn btn-outline-dark">See all frequently asked questions &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


